4. Carried from earlier plans: war as deaths per date block; Events for the Axial age and the democratic waves before 1945; dividing CO2, forest and sea level into processes."}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The people living in Sub-Saharan Africa is carved into 4 parts: The people living in Eastern Africa, The people living in Middle Africa, The people living in Southern Africa, The people living in Western Africa.

How the parts make the whole work: The four shares divide Sub-Saharan Africa's people at every date and sum to its share. Among foragers the continent's people were spread across all four, with Eastern and Southern Africa large; the Bantu-speaking farmers' spread from Middle Africa filled the east and south after 1000 BCE; the slave trades bled Western and Middle Africa most from 1650 to 1850 and conquest and the Congo Free State's regime struck Middle Africa again; since 1950 Eastern and Western Africa, with births still high, have grown fastest of all. Each part's turn comes at a different date, which Africa's one share hid.

Routing sample: 7 case(s); 0 with no home among the parts; 0 with two or more parts as homes.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-carve/v1","part":"synthesis","cutId":"carve.concept.humanity.africa.sub-saharan","conceptId":"concept.humanity.africa.sub-saharan","form":"processes","cutRecorded":true,"parts":[{"key":"eastern","conceptId":"concept.humanity.africa.sub-saharan.eastern","processId":"h.region-africa.sub-saharan.eastern"},{"key":"middle","conceptId":"concept.humanity.africa.sub-saharan.middle","processId":"h.region-africa.sub-saharan.middle"},{"key":"southern","conceptId":"concept.humanity.africa.sub-saharan.southern","processId":"h.region-africa.sub-saharan.southern"},{"key":"western","conceptId":"concept.humanity.africa.sub-saharan.western","processId":"h.region-africa.sub-saharan.western"}],"process":"h.region-africa.sub-saharan","routing":[{"case":"Omo Kibish in Ethiopia: Homo sapiens about 230,000 years ago","homes":["eastern"]},{"case":"Blombos Cave's engraved ochre, about 75,000 years ago","homes":["southern"]},{"case":"The Kingdom of Kongo, about 1390 to 1914","homes":["middle"]},{"case":"The Mali empire under Mansa Musa, about 1312 to 1337","homes":["western"]},{"case":"The rinderpest panzootic and the Ethiopian great famine, 1888 to 1892","homes":["eastern"]},{"case":"The Congo Free State, 1885 to 1908","homes":["middle"]},{"case":"The Witwatersrand gold rush draws migrant labour from across the region, from 1886","homes":["southern"]}]}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"Scale of rule is kept whole, as a kind of A dimension of rule: No carve of the largest polity's share pays now: the candidates were kinds (which polity is largest, from the Achaemenids to China and India; the empire's core against its subjects) or sibling readings of scale (the share held by the five largest polities, the effective number of polities, territory), none a part that sums to it. Reopen it when a series of the share under colonial rule from 1500 or of the whole size distribution of polities is opened, since scale would then be a parent with readings to divide, or when its Events or unexplained moves grow by half.

How the parts make the whole work: The largest polity's share is one order statistic of how humanity is divided among polities. It has no parts that sum to it: what changes within it is which polity is largest, a sequence of kinds the Events already tell, and, for empires, the split between core and subject peoples, recorded as the kind empire under scale.

Dropped: Core people and subject peoples, Which polity is largest, The rest of the size distribution, Territory held.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-carve/v1","part":"synthesis","cutId":"carve.concept.humanity.means.politics.scale","conceptId":"concept.humanity.means.politics.scale","form":"processes","cutRecorded":false,"parts":[],"process":"h.largest-polity"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The greatest settlement is kept whole, as a kind of A dimension of how a population settles: No carve of the largest city pays now: the candidates were kinds (which city), a matter of definition (core against suburbs, fixed here as the built-up area) or a sibling reading of the settlement pattern (the share of humanity in cities of a million or more), none a part that sums to it. Reopen when that share is opened under habitat, or when the Events that move the largest city or its unexplained moves grow by half.

How the parts make the whole work: The largest city's population is one order statistic of how humanity settles; its history is told by which city held the title and why it could be fed, which the Events carry. What it hides, the spread of great cities beyond the largest, is a sibling reading for habitat, not a part.

Dropped: Which city is largest, Core and suburbs, The other great cities.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-carve/v1","part":"synthesis","cutId":"carve.concept.humanity.means.habitat.largest-city","conceptId":"concept.humanity.means.habitat.largest-city","form":"processes","cutRecorded":false,"parts":[],"process":"h.largest-city"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"plan","text":"Done in this pass (2026-10-15, Meaning Model engine 0.13, Sema 0.10.0 with the project vocabulary store/sema/world-history.db). The model went from r95 (3401cfc2) to r157 (bb3c3d17). The graph was rebound to every model revision; from r101 to r125 it was rebound late, by the next carve, a lapse recorded in claude.finding.tree-pass-1.

The tree of processes went from 56 processes to 113. Every new process is a part of a recorded carve, with a measure, values over the whole span at all four levels of the time schedule, a band and a tag on every value, and a note where it turns. No existing process was filed under a new parent, and the six M49 areas and the existing measures keep their definitions.
- 28 carves are recorded with life_carve_record (frame, climb, the three tests for every candidate, completeness against an outside list, routed cases and synthesis). The first 15: history; humanity by place and by ends and means; Asia, the Americas, Latin America, Europe, Africa, Sub-Saharan Africa and Oceania into their M49 subregions; the Earth as setting; what matters to people; how people get it; staying alive; the causes of death. The next 13: meaning, sustenance, habitat, politics, provisioning, violence, war, the plant cover, voice, food, standing, connection, carbon dioxide.
- Two processes are kept whole with the reason recorded: the largest polity and the largest city.
- 57 processes are opened. Findings in claude.finding.tree-pass-1 and claude.finding.tree-pass-2.
- Values changed in existing measures: Bangladesh 1971 and Rwanda 1994 added to war and safety, the gap claude.plan.next-pass-8 named.

Left open, in order of what it would explain:
1. Re-filing, the choice this pass was told not to make. Kinds and second readings filed directly under a parent are flagged as untested parts: the eight religious shares (kinds of tradition, h.meaning.tradition), foraging (a kind of food-getting) and the food-work share (food-getting read by labour), both under h.provisioning, being online (a kind of moving words) under h.connection, and the development index under h.wants. So is the larger choice between the structure's twelve dimensions (acut.way-of-living) and the ends-and-means tree the measures hang on.
2. Divisions still without a recorded carve, each a single child: freedom (voice passed; civil liberties or women's legal autonomy would need a world series to make a second part), understanding (schooling; numeracy from age heaping is a candidate), belonging (marriage; extended-family or one-person households are candidates) and play (mass media; reading matter or the arts are candidates).
3. Frontier parts recorded with their verdicts, to promote when a world series can be read:
- the Earth: freshwater, nutrient cycles, methane and aerosols;
- the body: mental health;
- the means: know-how, the wealth stock, unpaid household work;
- meaning: the experience of the sacred, religious specialists;
- sustenance: clothing, household goods;
- the habitat: built land;
- politics: law, form of rule;
- violence: execution, which needs the safety measure widened, and violence that does not kill;
- the forests: open covers, planted against primary;
- freedom and voice: civil liberties;
- standing: women's standing, esteem;
- connection: migration.
Sibling readings worth opening: the share living in cities of a million or more, the share under colonial rule from 1500, the effective number of polities.
4. Value questions found and not settled:
- war's pre-modern peaks seem to include famine and disease deaths, which hunger and infection count, and war leaves out China's campaigns of 1950 to 1953 and the Cultural Revolution's killings;
- the forager child mortality against adult survival;
- Oceania's share from 1500 to 1800;
- energy for warmth counts food energy.
5. The deepen check continues with sea level (by ice sheet), government revenue, toil and exchange, and with the religious kinds once re-filed.
6. Coverage. The schedule is filled at all four levels for all 113 processes, but 105 processes pass over the model's own Events, above all 1940 to 1945 and 1960 to 1970. That is the coverage pass's work.
7. The repository. README.md and METHOD.md still describe the construction before the Americas pass, and construction/history-numbers.construction.json and construction/MANIFEST.json hold it at r58. Exporting with life_construction_export and updating both texts would publish this pass and the two before it.
8. Sources. Every reading is recalled; the first to check are the shares behind the new parts (output sectors, food sources, forest domains, wealth) and the death tolls behind the parts of war.
9. The model's unweighed causes: the Roman Empire, the Antarctic Treaty, the rise of Christianity, the French Revolution."}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"Water held on land is kept whole, as a kind of A reservoir of the Earth's water: The carve would pass, but it does not pay inside sea level now (MarginalValueRule#6611): dams and groundwater pumping are each a few centimetres of sea level since 1950 and nearly cancel, and natural storage before 1900 is guessed within a band of the same size. Their history is better followed as people's use of fresh water (water impounded, withdrawn and consumed), which has no home yet: the Earth's own carve should be asked whether fresh water is a part of it. Reopen when that fresh-water process is opened, or when the sea-level budget is followed year by year after 1950.

How the parts make the whole work: Water held on land stays one number within sea level. Its three budget terms pass the tests, but the human two are centimetres that nearly cancel, in a measure of metres, and their history belongs to people's use of fresh water rather than to sea level.

Frontier alternatives, kept with their verdicts for later evidence: Water impounded behind dams (declared), Groundwater pumped and not returned (declared), Natural storage: lakes, soils, snow, permafrost (declared).","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-carve/v1","part":"synthesis","cutId":"carve.concept.dim.earth.land-and-sea.land-water","conceptId":"concept.dim.earth.land-and-sea.land-water","form":"processes","cutRecorded":false,"parts":[],"process":"h.sea.land-water"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"Greenland's ice is kept whole, as a kind of A continental ice sheet: The carve would pass but does not pay now (MarginalValueRule#6611): the split between surface melt and discharge is measured only since the 1970s (discharge) and 1990s (surface balance from models and satellites); before that, and for the Last Interglacial's smaller sheet, it would be the parent's change divided by guess, and no human history in the account turns on which flow carried the loss. Reopen if the account follows the ice year by year after 1990, or extends past 2025.

How the parts make the whole work: Greenland's ice stays one number within sea level: its two budget terms pass the tests but are measured only since the 1970s and 1990s, and earlier they would be the parent's change split by guess.

Frontier alternatives, kept with their verdicts for later evidence: Ice lost or gained at the surface (declared), Ice lost by glaciers to the sea (declared).","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-carve/v1","part":"synthesis","cutId":"carve.concept.dim.earth.land-and-sea.greenland","conceptId":"concept.dim.earth.land-and-sea.greenland","form":"processes","cutRecorded":false,"parts":[],"process":"h.sea.greenland"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.region.americas (Events judged for those who follow the history of the Americas).
Answer: not modeled.

Most of the group is now linked, and the rest is not worth a new process. Of the 271 Events placed in the Americas, 154 now name the processes they change (r244 to r247), and the processes were given values where the links found them silent (r248 to r254), until the coverage report found none passing over its Events. What they change was already followed: the subregions' shares of humanity, the Americas' output, colonial rule, bondage and compelled work, war by kind, homicide, voice, foraging, freight, cropland, pasture, tropical forest, wild fish (the Grand Banks) and hereditary rank (the castas). The 131 judged for the Americas that stay unlinked fall into three kinds. (1) Below the resolution of world and M49 measures: a single city, chiefdom, massacre, treaty or doctrine (Cahokia, Chaco, Crow Creek, Mayapán, the Tarascan state, the Falklands, Tordesillas, the Monroe Doctrine, the Louisiana Purchase). (2) Carried by a linked Event: the Mississippian period carries the entradas, the Haitian Revolution Leclerc's expedition, the Second World War Pearl Harbor, the dictatorships Chile's coup and the Dirty War. (3) What they change has no process, and opening one does not pay now: change within Christianity (Pentecostal growth, liberation theology, the Great Awakening) moves people between traditions, not into or out of the faith, and would need a carve of the kept-whole h.religion-4; the missile crisis, a near miss, moves no measure. By the routing test (RoutingSanityCheck#71bd) every Event with a world-scale change found a home among existing processes, so no new process earns its keep for this region (MarginalValueRule#6611). Reopen if a regional history of the Americas is opened, where these Events would move the region's own measures.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.region.americas","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.americas"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.region.asia (Events judged for those who follow the history of Asia).
Answer: not modeled.

Most of the group is now linked, and the rest is not worth a new process. Of the 274 Events placed in Asia, 124 more now name the processes they change (r256 to r259), and values were added where the links found the processes silent (r260 to r269), until the coverage report again found none passing over its Events. Every kind of change the group showed already had a process: war deaths by kind (the Opium, Korean, Iran–Iraq, Indochina and Syrian wars, the Armenian genocide, the Cultural Revolution, Partition), hunger deaths (Bengal, the El Niño famines, northern Vietnam, the Soviet famine), colonial rule (the Company, the Raj, the VOC, French Indochina, Japan's Korea, the independences of 1946 to 1957), the largest polity and the share under a state (Akkad, Assyria, Maurya, Sui, Ming, Yuan), foraging (the Fertile Crescent, millet, rice, Mehrgarh, the Austronesian and mainland farmers), Asia's output (Japan's miracle, the tigers, the Asian crisis), extreme poverty (Doi Moi, the New Order, the region's escape from poverty), compelled work (the Cultivation System, the romusha, the Burma railway), bondage and rank (Joseon's slaves and yangban, the Vedic varnas, Siam's abolition), sea level (Sundaland), tropical forest (oil palm) and South-eastern Asia's share of humanity. About 126 judged for Asia stay unlinked: dynasties and courts whose change is in who rules rather than in any world measure (the Parthians, Sasanians, Seljuks, Kushans, Heian, Kamakura, Joseon's founding is linked but the Zhou conquest is not), single battles, sieges and treaties (Constantinople 1453, Bach Dang, Malacca's fall, the Six-Day War), cities and monuments (Angkor, Borobudur, Çatalhöyük, Göbekli Tepe), inventions whose world-scale effect comes through other Events (paper, printing, the Hangul alphabet, the house of wisdom) and archaic humans before Homo sapiens (the Denisovans, floresiensis, luzonensis, the last erectus), whom humanity's measures do not count. Change between branches of one faith (the Safavid turn to Shi'ism, Theravada's spread on the mainland) has no process, as for the Americas; following branches would need carving the kept-whole religion shares, which the coarse world measures do not reward now. By the routing test (RoutingSanityCheck#71bd) every Event with a world-scale change found a home, so no new process earns its keep here (MarginalValueRule#6611). Reopen if a regional history of Asia is opened.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.region.asia","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.asia"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.region.africa (Events judged for those who follow the history of Africa).
Answer: not modeled.

Most of the group is now linked, and the rest is not worth a new process. Of the Events judged for Africa, 63 more now name the processes they change (r271, r272), and values were added where the links found the processes silent (r273 to r278), until the coverage report again found none passing over its Events. Among them the transatlantic slave trade, which had named nothing, now names bondage, compelled work and the shares of Africa and the Americas; HIV/AIDS names infection deaths and life expectancy; Africa's periods name Africa's share of humanity; herding's spread names the share of mobile herders for the first time; rinderpest names the wild animals and hunger. What the group changes was already followed: war deaths by kind, hunger, colonial rule, the share under a state and the largest polity, foraging and herding, bondage and compelled work, rank and the vote (apartheid), Africa's output and extreme poverty, exchange and freight (the Suez Canal). The 73 still unlinked are kingdoms, courts and cities whose change is in who rules or what they built rather than in any world measure (Aksum, Kerma, Kush, Meroe, Great Zimbabwe, Mapungubwe, Ife, Igbo-Ukwu, Benin, Kongo, Asante, Oyo, the Almoravids and Almohads, the Fatimids, the Mamluks, the Solomonic line); single battles (Adwa, Tondibi, Mbwila); finds that date the species' early life but change no measure of humanity (the early fossils, Blombos, Pinnacle Point, the Bizmoune beads, Border Cave, the Ishango bone, the Khoe-San split); and Events carried by linked ones (the Second World War in Africa, the Cape Colony by colonial rule's count). Two kinds of change have no process: Christian and Muslim branches (Ethiopia's church, the Coptic split, Sufi orders), as for the Americas and Asia, and land dispossession within a country (the Natives Land Act's 7%), which a wealth-share measure at world scale cannot see. Neither earns a process at this resolution (MarginalValueRule#6611); every Event with a world-scale change found a home by the routing test (RoutingSanityCheck#71bd). Reopen if a regional history of Africa is opened.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.region.africa","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.africa"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.region.oceania (Events judged for those who follow the history of Oceania).
Answer: not modeled.

Most of what Oceania's Events change is now linked, and the rest is not worth a new process. 61 Events now name processes (r280, r281). Because Oceania's people are under one percent of humanity, most of them move Oceania's own subregions' shares (Australia and New Zealand, Melanesia, Micronesia, Polynesia), which every period, epidemic, voyage of settlement and wave of migration now names; others move world measures whose change happens here: the wild animals (Sahul's megafauna, the moa), wild sea mammals (the whalers and sealers) and wild fish (the island states' tuna zones), the first Events to name these last two; sea level (the atolls); colonial rule (the Pacific's partition and independence); foraging (New Guinea's gardens); pasture (the wool frontier); the Christian share; and the share of adults with the vote, through women's suffrage from New Zealand's 1893 on, which had named nothing. The 113 still unlinked are single islands' kingdoms and monuments (Nan Madol, Leluh, the latte, Rapa Nui's moai, Tonga's maritime chiefdom, Fiji's chiefdoms, the Pomare and Tupou kingdoms), exchange rings (the kula, the hiri, Yap's stone money) whose trade is a vanishing share of the world's, voyaging lore and arts (Hokule'a, the Festival of Pacific Arts, rugby), the nuclear tests (Castle Bravo, Moruroa: grave for the islanders but no world measure counts fallout), and political Events of countries of a few million (Federation, the Waitangi Tribunal, Fiji's coups, Bougainville), all below the resolution of world measures and carried for their region by the subregion shares. A process for nuclear contamination or for indigenous land held was considered and not opened: neither has a world-scale measure this model could fill honestly (MarginalValueRule#6611). By the routing test (RoutingSanityCheck#71bd) every Event with a world-scale change has a home. Reopen if a regional history of Oceania is opened.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.region.oceania","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.oceania"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.politics (Events judged for those who follow the history of politics).
Answer: modeled, followed by h.polities.

The group's Events, read whole, change four things. (1) Into how many units humanity is divided: unifications, partitions, breakups, independences, conquests of stateless peoples and the treaties of the states' system. No process followed this; the politics carve had merged it into scale. It is now followed by the count of autonomous polities (h.polities, opened r292 under h.politics after the carve was re-recorded at r291) and its kind, independent states (h.polities.states), and 25 Events name them (r293): the Zhou enfeoffments, the poleis, Qin, the Mongols, Constantinople, Westphalia, the fiscal-military state, the partitions of Poland, the American and Latin American independences, Vienna, Liberia, the unifications of Italy and Germany, the Berlin conference and the Scramble, Versailles, Israel, decolonization, the year of Africa, the Caribbean's and the Pacific's independences, the Soviet and Yugoslav breakups and Timor-Leste. (2) Who rules and how far: already followed by colonial rule, the largest polity, the share under a state and voice, which earlier passes and this one linked (the Atlantic revolutions, the Roman Republic, Athens, fascism, the Iron Curtain, India's democracy). (3) Fighting over rule: war by kind. (4) What remains unlinked, about 169 Events, is mostly the form of rule and its constraints: revolutions that replace one kind of ruler with another (Iran 1979), coups (Chile 1973), constitutions and charters (Magna Carta, the Glorious Revolution, the secret ballot), dynasties and courts, and treaties that order relations among states without changing their number (the Antarctic Treaty, the Monroe Doctrine). The politics carve keeps the form of rule (a Cut of regime types) and law and justice as frontier alternatives; following them needs that Cut, which this pass does not open (MarginalValueRule#6611). Reopen when a series of regime types is opened.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.politics","answer":"modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.politics","process":"h.polities"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.security (Events judged for those who follow the history of security).
Answer: modeled, followed by h.means.force.arms.

Read whole, the group's Events that named nothing were mostly about the means of war, which the account held only as people under arms: gunpowder, the atomic bombs, the hydrogen-bomb tests, the arms race, the world wars' economies and the peace dividend. Force had never been carved; it now is (carve.concept.humanity.means.force, r300), with two parts opened at r301 and valued over the whole span: arms, the energy of the most destructive weapon in service (h.means.force.arms), and spending on force as a share of world output (h.means.force.spending), with nuclear warheads as a kind of arms (h.means.force.arms.nuclear). Eleven Events now name them or war (r303): gunpowder, nuclear weapons, Hiroshima, Castle Bravo, the Pacific tests, both world wars, the fiscal-military state, the end of the Cold War, the Long Peace and the Crusades. What stays unlinked, about 75 Events, is of three kinds. (1) Single battles, sieges and raids carried by the wars that hold them (Pearl Harbor by the Pacific war, Gallipoli by the First World War, Tet and Dien Bien Phu by the Indochina wars, Adwa, Tondibi, Mbwila, Bach Dang). (2) Coups and seizures of power (Chile 1973, Guatemala 1954), which change the form of rule, a frontier of the politics carve, more than any measure of force. (3) Near misses and doctrines that change no measure (the Cuban missile crisis, the Monroe Doctrine). None earns a process at this resolution (MarginalValueRule#6611); reopen with a Cut of regime types, or if a regional history is opened.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.security","answer":"modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.security","process":"h.means.force.arms"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.region.europe (Events judged for those who follow the history of Europe).
Answer: not modeled.

Most of the group is now linked, and the rest is not worth a new process. Of the 87 Events placed in Europe that named no process, 50 now name the processes they change (r285, r286) and seven more name the counts of states and polities (r293); with the world Events linked at r284 and values added where the links found processes silent (r287 to r290), the coverage report again finds none passing over its Events. What they change was already followed, or is now: war by kind, contestation, the vote and rank, compelled work, revenue and its bases, spending on force, trade and Europe's output, making and the urban share, passenger speed and freight, infection, hunger, higher learning, sea level and the ice, Europe's share and, for the first time, its four subregions' shares (the emigration, the expulsions, the Irish famine, the Mongols in Rus', the poleis, the Vikings, the Thirty Years' War). The 24 still unlinked are Europe's eras (carried by the Events inside them), courts and dynasties (Byzantium, the Franks, al-Andalus, the Ottoman Balkans), ideas without a process of discovery (the Renaissance, the Enlightenment, Greek philosophy, the scientific revolution), art and monuments (Aurignacian art, the megaliths, the Minoan and Mycenaean palaces), Neanderthals (not counted by humanity's measures), single eruptions, charters (Magna Carta, the Glorious Revolution), the witch hunts (about 100,000 dead over more than a century, under a hundredth of a death per 100,000 a year at world scale) and the Great Schism (a change between branches of one faith). The making of new knowledge is the one kind with no home: the carve of how people get it keeps it as a frontier, and the knowledge group of the breadth check will ask for it on its own; it is not opened for Europe's sake (MarginalValueRule#6611). Reopen if a regional history of Europe is opened.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.region.europe","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.europe"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.region.antarctica (Events judged for those who follow the history of Antarctica).
Answer: not modeled.

Most of the group is now linked, and the rest is not worth a new process. Antarctica's history in this account is 14 Events, and 9 of them now name what they change (model r339). (1) How much of Antarctica's ice-free land is within human reach (h.habitat.range.antarctica, opened at r337 as a part of range): the sighting (1820), the exploration era, the heroic age, the IGY's stations, the treaty and the treaty era. It is zero before 1820 and about 0.03% of the world's land now. (2) Antarctica's ice (h.sea.antarctic, its part of sea level, kept whole at r228): the glacial cycles before 9700 BCE, the ice loss from 1992 and the treaty era. (3) The wild sea mammals (h.earth.wild-animals.sea-mammals): sealing and whaling from 1820 to 1986 and the exploration era, so the Southern Ocean's whaling, the largest single taking of sea-mammal mass, is observed where it happened. The other five are not followed, each for a reason. The untouched era has no people, so nothing human changes. The race to the South Pole was inland on the ice, outside the ice-free land range counts; its home would be exploration, which this account follows only through discovery's researchers. The territorial claims, over land with no residents, change no measure here: colonial rule counts people, and no count of polities changes. The Madrid Protocol bans mining that never existed, so nothing it changes is measured. The ozone hole falls under stratospheric ozone, which has no process; it is answered with the Earth group. A process for any of them would hold one flat line with one Event on it.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.region.antarctica","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.region.antarctica"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.beliefs (Events judged for those who follow the history of beliefs and norms).
Answer: not modeled.

Partly linked, and the rest not followed now, with one candidate named for the next pass. Seven of the group's Events now name what they change (model r352). The conversions move the tradition shares: Aksum's turn to Christianity (h.religion-4 from h.religion-0), Indic kingship in South-east Asia (h.religion-1 and -2 from -0), Dvaravati and the Theravada mainland (h.religion-2, from Hindu courts), and the Jesuit missions among the Guaraní (h.religion-4 from -0). Two revivals that change worship within a tradition move regular worship (h.meaning): the Great Awakening and the Pentecostal rise in Latin America, which leaves the Christian share as it was. The other Events change things no measure here follows, and none of them forms a group a new world measure would carry well. Monuments and ritual centres (Göbekli Tepe, Sechin Alto, Lalibela) say that people built for the sacred, not how many worshipped or what they believed. Persecutions (the witch-hunts, about 40,000 to 60,000 executed over a century) are too few in deaths to move a world rate, and their judicial killing sits between homicide and one-sided killing as this account defines them. Movements inside one tradition (liberation theology, Melanesia's cargo cults and churches) change neither the shares nor worship measurably. Short-lived reforms (Akhenaten's Aten) left no lasting share. The candidate worth opening next is the people kept for worship: monks, nuns, priests and temple staff per thousand people, a sibling of discovery's people kept for inquiry, which would give desert monasticism, the sangha's monasteries, the Reformation's dissolutions and secularization a measure; it is left for the next pass because it belongs under regular worship (h.meaning), whose carve still holds the eight tradition shares as untested parts that the closing note of fill-widen-2 says should move or be carved again, and this pass keeps the existing measures where they hang.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.beliefs","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.beliefs"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.earth (Events judged for those who follow the history of the Earth as humanity's setting).
Answer: not modeled.

Partly linked, and the rest not followed now. At model r339 and r354 seven of the group's Events came to name what they change: Antarctica's ice loss and glacial cycles (h.sea.antarctic), sealing and whaling (h.earth.wild-animals.sea-mammals), the Americas' megafauna extinction (h.earth.wild-animals), the ice-free corridor (range in the Americas), the Black Summer fires (h.forest.temperate) and Tōhoku (h.alive.injury). What is left are mostly single eruptions (the Campanian Ignimbrite, Thera, Hunga Tonga), whose effects on the world's measures are either brief and within the bands of global temperature as this account samples it, or argued (the Campanian eruption's effect on Europe's people); the spread of wild cereals before farming, which the plant cover's measures by climate zone do not separate; Aboriginal fire on the land, whose effect on Australia's vegetation is debated; and the ozone hole. The one candidate worth a process is stratospheric ozone over Antarctica in spring, in Dobson units: flat near 300 for all of human history, falling to about 100 in the 1990s and recovering slowly after the Montreal Protocol; it would be one curve with two Events on it and a long flat line, so it waits until the account follows the atmosphere's composition beyond carbon dioxide.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.earth","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.earth"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.knowledge (Events judged for those who follow the history of knowledge).
Answer: not modeled.

Partly linked, and the rest not followed now, with the candidate that would take them named. With discovery opened by area this pass (r347, r348), the group's Events of inquiry now name the part for their area: the Museum's Alexandria, the House of Wisdom, Greek philosophy, the universities, the scientific revolution, the Enlightenment, Apollo and American computing (r349), and Ibn Khaldun's Muqaddimah and Mesoamerica's first writing and calendars (r356). What remains is mostly about how knowledge is stored and copied: paper in Han China, woodblock printing, Hangul, the alphabet. Literacy (h.understanding) already takes the ones that changed who could read; the others change the cost and durability of keeping knowledge, which is the frontier part 'knowledge held in store' of the understanding carve (r326), kept frontier because no world series of books or texts per person can be read before about 1500 outside Europe and China. Tasmania's isolation, the loss of skills in a small cut-off population (CumulativeCulture#4f93), has no world measure: it is a regional case of the mechanism, best followed if a local history of Tasmania is opened. Reopen this group when a series of book production (Buringh and van Zanden for Europe, with China's and the Islamic world's estimates) is checked.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.knowledge","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.knowledge"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.population (Events judged for those who follow the history of population).
Answer: not modeled.

Mostly linked, and the rest not followed. The population group's migrations and peoplings were linked in the stopped pass and in this one (to migration and range and their area parts, r330, r339, r345). At r358 four more name what they change: the Ebola epidemic and Leclerc's yellow fever (deaths from infection), the opioid epidemic (deaths from injury, counted as poisonings) and de Soto's and Coronado's expeditions (the people of Northern America). What is left is about descent rather than number: the deep splits of human lineages that genomes record (the Khoe-San branching off about 300,000 to 200,000 years ago, and others like it). They change how humanity's ancestry is structured, which no measure here follows; a process for it (for example the share of living people's ancestry from each deep lineage) would need a genomic reconstruction this account cannot sketch honestly at world scale. Reopen if the account follows ancestry or admixture as its own measure.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.population","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.population"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.habitat (Events judged for those who follow the history of habitat).
Answer: not modeled.

Not followed now, with the candidate that would take most of them named. As the check's examples show (Çatalhöyük, Great Zimbabwe, Cahokia), the group's unlinked Events are single towns and their monuments, mostly of 5,000 to 30,000 people. Habitat as this account follows it is world measures: the share living in towns (h.habitat), the greatest settlement (h.largest-city), settling down (h.habitat.mobile), farmland and range with its area parts; a town of 15,000 moves none of them by a visible amount, and the first peoplings and abandonments that do move range were linked this pass (r339, r354). The process that would give such Events a home is the number of cities and towns above a threshold (for example cities of 100,000 or more, from Chandler's, Modelski's and Reba and colleagues' reconstructions), which follows urban networks that the urban share and the largest city hide; at 100,000 it would still miss these towns, and at 10,000 its early counts would be guesses of a few dozen. It is left for a pass that checks one of those reconstructions. Reopen when it is opened or when a regional history (Mesoamerica, the Mississippi, the Zimbabwe plateau) is opened by encapsulation.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.habitat","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.habitat"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.arts (Events judged for those who follow the history of the arts and play).
Answer: modeled, followed by h.play.makers.

Read whole, the 25 Events of the arts and play that named no process change two things the model did not follow. (1) Whether populations make lasting art at all: Bizmoune's shells, Blombos, the Aurignacian, Sulawesi, Aboriginal rock art and the Gravettian's spread now name image and ornament (h.play.images), and the Sahara's rock art observes it. (2) How many people are kept to make the arts for courts, temples and markets: the Olmec, Nok, Igbo-Ukwu, Ife, Lalibela, Borobudur, the Gupta, Heian, Minoan Crete, Dong Son, Paracas and Nazca, Rapa Nui's carvers, the Renaissance, the Festival of Pacific Arts, rugby's professional players and the sack of Benin now name the arts' makers (h.play.makers), and Benin colonial rule too. Both were opened from the re-recorded carve of beauty and play (r363) with values at every date of the schedule (r364, r366). Left unlinked, each for its reason: the signs of Neanderthal minds (Neanderthals are not counted among the living people these shares divide), the Amazon's early pottery (no measure follows pottery), the Mokaya ball court (games and sport are a frontier part of the carve, without a world measure), and the Magdalenians, who already name Europe's people.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.arts","answer":"modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.arts","process":"h.play.makers"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.society (Events judged for those who follow the history of society).
Answer: modeled, followed by h.understanding.languages.

Ten of the society group's Events named no process. Eight now name what they change (r386): the New Laws and Palmares change the share held in bondage; the Cape Colony changes colonial rule in Africa and bondage; blackbirding changes compelled work and migration into Oceania; the 'social laboratory' changes the terms of work for an employer; Maori Aotearoa extends Oceania's range and people. Residential schools and the stolen generations took children from their languages, which no process followed; the count of living languages (h.understanding.languages) now follows it, opened as the language part of the carve of Understanding (r384, r385), which had named language as missing, and the language-family Events (Bantu, Austronesian, Pama-Nyungan, the steppe migrations, the Taino) are linked to it too. Two remain, for reasons: the Seneca Falls convention changes no measure in 1848, and its consequence is followed through the women's vote (ev.womens-suffrage on h.voice.suffrage); the Caribbean labour rebellions change unions and labour law, which no measure follows, and their consequences, adult suffrage from 1944 and independence, lie in later Events. The candidate if this group grows: union membership as a share of workers, under work for an employer, which would also take the European labour movement and the New Deal (MarginalValueRule#6611).","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.society","answer":"modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.society","process":"h.understanding.languages"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.provisioning (Events judged for those who follow the history of provisioning).
Answer: not modeled.

This pass linked the group's other Events (r378): the horse on the Plains, the north-west coast, the green Sahara's fishers, Budj Bim, Australia's mid-Holocene, the Hohokam canals, the Special Period, Folsom and El Fin del Mundo, with Jerimalai, Pinnacle Point, Border Cave and the Hoabinhians as observations. Four remain: three independent inventions of pottery (East Asia's foragers about 18,000 years ago, Ounjougou in the Sahara about 9400 BCE, the Amazon) and the bow's spread in the eastern woodlands. What they change is real, cooking by boiling, storage and softer food for the young and old, and for the bow the reach of hunting and raiding, but no measure here would move with them at world scale beyond what settling down (h.habitat.mobile), foraging (h.foraging) and the food measures already follow: pottery spreads with settled life almost everywhere, and its exceptions (pottery before farming in East Asia and the Sahara, the aceramic Neolithic of the Levant, Polynesians who gave pottery up) are cases, not a trajectory. The measure that would follow them, the share of people in pottery-making communities, is named for a carve of provisioning's tools if the group's evidence grows (MarginalValueRule#6611, AbsenceEvidence#10a3: the absence of pots in an assemblage is weak evidence of their absence in use).","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.provisioning","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.provisioning"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.connection (Events judged for those who follow the history of connection).
Answer: not modeled.

This pass linked the group's other Events (r378, r386): camels and the Sahara's freight, the Norse in Greenland, Zheng He, the New Guinea highland patrols, Cook in Polynesia and Spain in the Marianas, with Ibn Battuta and the race to the South Pole as observations of the state they show. Three remain, each a first contact or a claim that changes no state the model measures when it happens: Cabral's claim (1500) brings no one under rule until settlement and sugar from the 1530s, which Brazil's sugar Event and colonial rule in the Americas follow; the Dutch landfalls on New Holland and Aotearoa (1606 to 1644) bring neither settlement nor trade, and Australia's colonial history begins in 1788; the Polynesian meeting with South Americans (about 1200) moved a crop and some genes, not goods or people at a scale any connection measure reads, and its consequence, the sweet potato across Polynesia and Aotearoa, is in their Events. The measure that would follow them is the share of humanity in societies in regular contact with another continent, which would rise in steps at 1492, 1521 and the Pacific voyages; it is named for later, if the group grows (MarginalValueRule#6611, ContrastClass#7398: a first contact matters by what follows it, not by itself).","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.connection","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.connection"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.causes-of-death.violence.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of violence (r136) left two things without a home. (1) Killing by a group's own rule: judicial and customary executions (and among foragers the collective killing of a dangerous member), the sacrifice of retainers and captives (Ur's royal tombs, Kerma, the Shang, the Aztec temples), and killings by police. It passes the tests once the frame is deliberate killing: necessary (the witch-hunts' 40,000 to 60,000 executions, Tudor and Qing justice, the Aztec sacrifices, the abolition of the death penalty in most countries since 1960 have no home), independent (it fell in Europe after 1750 on its own timetable) and universal (every society puts some of its members to death). It is not followed now for one reason only: the carve divides violent death as the parent measures it, homicide plus war (h.safety), and that measure leaves these deaths out, so a part opened under it would not be part of what its parent counts; widening h.safety is a change to an existing measure, which this pass leaves as it is. Political mass executions (the Great Terror, the Khmer Rouge's) are already counted under one-sided killing (h.war.one-sided.states), and policy famines under hunger. The measure that would follow the rest is named for the pass that widens h.safety: killing by a group's own rule, per 100,000 living people a year, sketched at perhaps 1 to 5 among foragers (Boehm and Wrangham on collective execution), higher in the first states with retainer and captive sacrifice, about 4 per 100,000 of the world's people from the Aztec sacrifices alone in the fifteenth century, a European peak about 1550 to 1650, and under 0.5 since 1950 (a few thousand executions a year, most in China and Iran, and some tens of thousands of police killings). The Events it would take are already in the model (the witch-hunts, the Sumerian city-states' and Kerma's sacrificed retainers, the French Revolution's executions). (2) Violence that does not kill (assault, rape, torture, the beating of wives and children) lies outside the carve's frame, which is violence as a cause of death, and no world measure reads it before victimization surveys of the late twentieth century; it is the frame's boundary, not a missing part (AbsenceEvidence#10a3: silence in older records is not its absence). MarginalValueRule#6611.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.causes-of-death.violence","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.violence"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.dim.earth.wild-animals.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of the wild animals (r327) left wild birds, arthropods and the other invertebrates, and the small fish of the ocean's twilight zone without a home. All three pass necessity and independence (island bird extinctions after human arrival, the moa and the dodo; the recent fall of farmland birds and the insect-decline debate; the mesopelagic fish untouched until lately), but none can yet carry a world measure across the span: wild bird biomass has world estimates only from about 1970 (Bar-On, Phillips and Milo give about 2 Mt C now; North America lost about 29% of its birds from 1970 to 2017 by Rosenberg and colleagues), insect biomass trends are local and disputed (Hallmann and colleagues against van Klink and colleagues), and twilight-zone fish are uncertain within a factor of ten now. A series from 300,000 years ago would be guesses about guesses, adding no turn the land mammals, sea mammals and fish already show: losses by island colonization and hunting, then by land use and industrial fishing. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611, AbsenceEvidence#10a3); reopen when a world bird series before 1970 or a checked insect trend is read, or when island extinctions are followed as a count of species lost.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.dim.earth.wild-animals","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.wild-animals"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.ends-means.
Answer: modeled, followed by h.means.force.

The carve of humanity into ends and means (r103) left two things without a home, and both have one now, so the carve's completeness is answered by later carves rather than by carving it again. (1) The means of organized violence as a means rather than a toll: followed since r109 by force (h.means.force, people under arms per 1,000), a part of how people get it, and since r300 by its parts, the destructive power of weapons (h.means.force.arms, with nuclear warheads as a kind) and spending on force (h.means.force.spending). (2) The making of new knowledge: followed since r328 by discovery (h.understanding.discovery, people kept to make new knowledge per million), with its five parts by area since r347; it is filed under understanding, an end, because knowledge is sought for itself as well as for what it makes possible, and its use as a means (the research laboratory's inventions, war research) is a seam with provisioning and force, recorded on discovery's carve (r346). The carve of humanity itself stays as recorded (two parts, the ends and the means); no part is missing from it, and the twelve dimensions of the structure construction remain a rival carve of the same whole, the open choice this pass does not make.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.ends-means","answer":"modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.humanity","process":"h.means.force"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.means.force.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of force (r300) left two things without a home. (1) How fighters are raised and held (warrior bands and kin, levies and militias, mercenaries and standing professionals, conscripts, volunteers) is not a part beside people under arms, arms and spending but a division of the people under arms themselves: categories competing for one pool, which belong in a Cut series on the fighters, read at every block of the time schedule, not in a number. It is named for a pass that records series: 'How do the world's people under arms divide by how they were raised?', answers kin and warrior bands, levies and militias, paid professionals and mercenaries, conscripts, volunteers; expected to be nearly all warrior bands before states, levies and militias in the agrarian empires with professional cores (Rome's legions, the Ottoman janissaries), conscripts from the levee en masse of 1793 to the 1970s, and volunteers again in most rich states since. (2) Protection (walls, forts, armour) fails universality as a part: many bands built no defences, so it is a kind of force found where people are settled; and no world series of fortification can be stated. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611).","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.means.force","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.force"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.means.habitat.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of habitat (r325) left built-up land and public works (the area under buildings, streets and works, and the water, sewer and power networks of settlements) without a home. Its independence passes (urban densities have fallen for two centuries, so built land grows apart from the urban share, as Angel's Planet of Cities shows), but before satellite mapping from 1975 the world's built-up area is reconstructed from urban population times assumed densities (HYDE's built-up layer is made that way), so a series before 1975 would restate the urban share and the largest city rather than add a reading of its own; and mobile foragers build almost nothing that lasts, which leaves its universality uncertain. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611, MetricReading#56a9: a measure derived from another is not a second reading of the world). Reopen when an independent reconstruction of built area before 1975 is checked (archaeological site areas for the ancient cities, cadastral maps for the early modern), or when sanitation and water supply are followed as shares of people served, which do have readings from about 1850.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.means.habitat","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.habitat"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.means.politics.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of politics (r291) left law and justice and the form of rule without a home. (1) The form of rule (who rules and how they are chosen: no state, chiefly or royal rule, oligarchic and aristocratic republics, party states, democracies, rule from overseas) passes necessity and independence, but its categories compete for one pool, the world's people, so it belongs in a Cut series, not a number; it is the most rewarding opening the breadth check has left, and is named for the next pass: 'How do the world's living people divide by the kind of highest authority they live under?', answers no state, monarchy or chiefly rule over a state, non-elected republic or oligarchy, party or military state, electoral democracy, colonial rule from overseas, read at every block of the time schedule with readings nested coarse to fine. Its long course is already constrained by measures the account holds: the share under no state is the complement of h.politics, colonial rule is h.colonial, and democracies are h.voice, so the series must agree with them. It is not recorded now because a nested series over all four levels of the schedule, consistent with three existing measures, is a pass's work in itself. (2) Law and justice (codes, courts, the rule of law) has a world reading only from 1789 (V-Dem's rule of law index); before that a share living under written law would restate the share living under a state. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611).","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.means.politics","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.politics"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of what matters to people (r107) left two of Nussbaum's capabilities without a home of their own. (1) Holding property on an equal basis with others: the account now follows the wealth people hold as a means (h.means.wealth, opened at r419) and who holds it under standing (h.standing.wealth, the richest tenth's share), so what the capability asks, how equally assets are held, is read by the second; a separate end would count it twice. (2) Concern for other species and the natural world: a real end in many traditions, but no world measure of it can be stated that is not a measure of the living world itself (forest, the wild animals, sea mammals, fish) or of a modern practice (protected areas, about 17% of land by 2020, with readings only from about 1960). Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611); reopen if the share of land under protection is opened as a measure of the living world's care, with the sacred groves and hunting reserves of earlier centuries as its older kinds. (Recorded again on the main line: an identical answer was first registered in parallel from the same parent as the politics answer, on a side branch, model 41ffd0d2, which no graph follows.)","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.wants"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.alive.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of staying alive and well (r121) left the years lived in ill health and disability, and mental health, without a home. Both pass necessity and independence, but neither has a world reading before the Global Burden of Disease study's series from 1990 (healthy life expectancy, disability-adjusted life years, the burden of depression and anxiety); before that, a value would be life expectancy times a guessed fraction, a restatement of survival rather than a reading of ill health. The body's condition in earlier centuries is read through stature (h.health) and the causes of death, which carry what can be said. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611, AbsenceEvidence#10a3: that the past left few records of suffering is no evidence of its absence). Reopen if healthy life expectancy is opened from 1990 with a sketched course before it bounded by stature and morbidity studies of past populations (skeletal lesions, enamel defects), which bioarchaeology can supply.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.alive","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.alive"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.belonging.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of belonging (r213) left voluntary associations (guilds, confraternities, clubs, unions, parties, foragers' sodalities and age sets) without a home. They pass necessity and independence (they grow as kin groups dissolve), but no world measure of membership can be read back before the twentieth century; the one candidate with readings, union membership as a share of workers (from about 1880 in the industrial countries, the ILO's from about 1950), was named by the society group's breadth answer (r390) and would sit under work for an employer, not belonging. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611); reopen with that union series, or when guild and confraternity membership in early modern European and Chinese cities is read as a share of townspeople.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.belonging","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.belonging"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.meaning.
Answer: modeled, followed by h.means.devotion.

The carve of meaning (r127) left two of Smart's dimensions of religion without a measured home. (1) The institutional dimension (full-time religious specialists and the bodies that keep them: temples, churches, the sangha, the ulama) was kept as a frontier part 'worth opening if a series of full-time religious specialists per 1,000 people can be read'. It is now followed by organized belief (h.means.devotion), opened at r419 as a part of how people get it, the counterpart of force's people under arms (Mann's ideological power), with values from 300,000 years ago to 2025 and linked to the first monastic orders, Christian monasticism, Buddhism's spread east, the Tang's suppression, Pagan and the Theravada monasteries, the Reformation, the French and Russian revolutions and the communist suppressions; meaning keeps the end, the share taking part in worship, and the seam between them is recorded on both carves. (2) The experience of the sacred (trance, visions, mystical states, prayer felt as answered) still has no world measure across the span, since surveys of religious experience begin in the twentieth century; it stays a frontier alternative of meaning's carve.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.meaning","answer":"modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.meaning","process":"h.means.devotion"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.play.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of beauty and play (r363) left three things without a measured home. (1) The forms that leave no lasting trace before writing (music, dance, story) are in every population but no world measure can read them across the span; their makers, once kept, are counted among the arts' makers (now divided by who keeps them, r397), and their audiences, once copied, in mass media. (2) What people spend on feasts, festivals and entertainment has household-budget readings only from about 1900. (3) Games and sport: their paid players are counted among the arts' makers (markets, since the codification of football and rugby), the hours played are leisure, and organized contests with fixed rules and audiences are a kind many populations lack. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611, AbsenceEvidence#10a3); reopen if festival and holy days a year are opened as a count beside leisure hours, which has readings for the medieval calendars and the Protestant cuts in them.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.play","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.play"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.standing.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of standing (r150) left women's standing against men and esteem (how people feel they stand) without a measured home. Women's standing passes necessity and independence, but no world measure of it reaches back before the 1990s (the gender development and inequality indices) or, for law, before V-Dem's women's civil liberties index from 1789; parts of it are already read elsewhere (women's vote under voice, women's age at marriage, plural unions). Esteem is a reading of persons with no world series at all. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611). The candidate most worth opening is women's legal standing, the share of the world's women living where married women can own property and sue in their own name, which has a clear course (coverture's laws repealed from 1839 to the 1970s, Islamic and customary law's own rules) and Events in the account (the women's vote, Seneca Falls); it would sit under freedom beside voice.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.standing","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.standing"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.sustenance.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of sustenance and comfort (r129) left clothing and household goods without a measured home. Clothing: a world series of textile fibre per person exists from about 1900; before that, cotton's spread and the industrial revolution's cheap cloth are well told but would be sketched as one number per person with bands wider than the change, and its comfort is mostly warmth, which energy already carries. Household goods: the consumer and industrious revolutions are read in probate inventories and household surveys for some places and times only. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611); reopen if fibre per person is opened from 1900 with its earlier course bounded by Europe's and China's textile output (Riello, Broadberry), which would also give the cotton revolution's Events (Lancashire, the cotton gin, India's handloom collapse) a measure to move.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.sustenance","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.sustenance"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.understanding.
Answer: not modeled.

The carve of understanding (r384) left knowledge held in store (books, archives, libraries: knowledge kept outside heads) as a frontier part, for universality uncertain. It passes necessity and independence (book production rose apart from literacy), but a world series of books or titles per person can be read only from about 1450 in Europe (Buringh and van Zanden) and for Song and later China in pieces; before printing, manuscripts and tablets are counted only for a few libraries; and after 2000 books are a falling share of what is stored, so one measure would change its meaning midway (MetricReading#56a9: one definition must hold over the series). Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611). The candidate, if opened, is new titles printed per million people a year from 1450, with Europe's and China's series summed and the rest of the world sketched; Printing in East Asia and printing with movable type in Europe, already Events of the account, would name it.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"gap:carve.concept.humanity.wants.understanding","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.gap.understanding"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:importance.dim.exchange (Events judged for those who follow the history of exchange).
Answer: not modeled.

The stopped pass linked the exchange group's other Events (r377). One remains: mobile money in Africa, from M-Pesa in 2007. It changes how payments move and who can make them (Kenya's households reached by a phone-based account, and the remittances sent home that way), which no measure of the account follows: trade between peoples (h.exchange) does not see it, the share online (h.internet) does not count the feature phones it runs on, and its effect on extreme poverty, about 2% of Kenyan households by Suri and Jack's study, does not show at world scale. Not followed now (MarginalValueRule#6611). The measure that would follow it is the share of the world's adults with an account at a bank or a mobile-money provider (the World Bank's Findex, from 2011: about half then, three quarters by 2021), which would also take the savings banks and credit societies of earlier centuries as its older kinds.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:importance.dim.exchange","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.events.importance.dim.exchange"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:within:ev.af.era.msa.
Answer: linked.

The one Event within Africa's Middle Stone Age that named no process, Still Bay and Howiesons Poort (about 77,000 to 59,000 years ago), now observes image and ornament (h.play.images, r436): its engraved ochre and ostrich eggshell and shell beads show southern African populations making lasting art, and its toolkits' fading and return is the flicker that measure's bands hold (CumulativeCulture#4f93). Its hafted microliths and heat treatment change technique, which the account follows only through what techniques do (the structure construction's rejection of technology as a dimension), so no further link is made.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:within:ev.af.era.msa","answer":"linked","conceptId":"breadth.events.within.msa"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:within:ev.age.agrarian.
Answer: linked.

The one Event within the agrarian age that named no process, the era of the first farmers (9700 to 3500 BCE), now names farmland (h.farmland), the share living by foraging (h.foraging), the share without a fixed dwelling (h.habitat.mobile) and nitrogen fixed by people (h.earth.nitrogen) (r438): the world-scale changes its description names, as farming peoples spread and absorb foragers. Its finer Events (each centre of domestication, Catalhoyuk, the first copper) already carry their own links.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:within:ev.age.agrarian","answer":"linked","conceptId":"breadth.events.within.agrarian"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named events:within:ev.life.earth.
Answer: linked.

The one Event within the Earth's lifecycle that named no process, the spread of wild cereal stands across the Levant and the Zagros (about 12,700 to 9700 BCE), now observes global temperature (h.earth) and carbon dioxide (h.co2) (r440), the warming and the rising carbon dioxide under which the founder crops' ancestors grew densely within people's reach. The stands themselves are grassland and open woodland, which the plant cover's measure (forest) does not count; a measure of grassland or of wild cereal range is not worth opening for one Event (MarginalValueRule#6611). The Event is already a cause of the Fertile Crescent's farming in the account's causes.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"events:within:ev.life.earth","answer":"linked","conceptId":"breadth.events.within.earth"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"The breadth check named remainder:cut.columbian.deaths-by-cause:other_epidemics.
Answer: not modeled.

The Cut dividing the deaths beyond ordinary mortality among the peoples of the Americas from 1492 to 1650 by what killed them (cut.columbian.deaths-by-cause) gives 0.42 to 'other epidemics', a named answer, not a remainder, but one that holds several diseases. Read as recalled, it divides roughly: cocoliztli, the epidemics of 1545 to 1548 and 1576 to 1580 that may have killed half or more of central Mexico's surviving people, perhaps a third of the answer; measles (from 1531, again in the 1590s), perhaps a quarter; typhus (matlazahuatl), perhaps a sixth; influenza (1558 to 1559), perhaps a tenth; malaria and yellow fever, which arrive with enslaved Africans and strike the Caribbean and coasts from the 1640s, perhaps a tenth; mumps, diphtheria and pertussis the rest. What cocoliztli was is debated (EvidenceUnderdetermination#999b): Salmonella enterica Paratyphi C, an enteric fever brought from Europe, on the ancient DNA from Teposcolula-Yucundaa (Vagene and colleagues 2018); a native haemorrhagic fever amplified by the megadrought of the 1540s and 1570s (Acuna-Soto and colleagues 2002); or both at once. A conditioned division would need the parent recorded as a series, which it is not (it was registered as a single Cut on ev.columbian-exchange), and its shares would be guesses inside a guess; not recorded now (MarginalValueRule#6611). Reopen when the parent is recorded as a series, or when the epidemics are read decade by decade for central Mexico and the Andes, where the counts of tributaries allow it.","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-breadth-record/v1","candidate":"remainder:cut.columbian.deaths-by-cause:other_epidemics","answer":"not_modeled","conceptId":"breadth.remainder.columbian.other-epidemics"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"Mobile herders is kept whole, as a kind of Settling down: people without a fixed dwelling: No carve pays now. The regional split is the only candidate that passes necessity and independence, but every value of the whole is sketched or wide, and no source counts herders by region before about 1950, so its parts would be guesses dividing a guess. Reopen when regional herder counts are entered: national censuses of pastoralists since 1950 (Mongolia, Kenya, Somalia, Sudan, Saudi Arabia) or the Ethnographic Atlas coded by region and date.

How the parts make the whole work: Kept whole. The herders are under one person in a hundred at their peak and about half a percent now. Their Events (the steppe empires, the camel in Arabia and the Sahara, Kazakh collectivization, the Sahel droughts, rinderpest) can be noted on the whole, as they are. Splitting it would multiply sketched numbers without adding evidence (EvidenceUnderdetermination#999b; MarginalValueRule#6611).

Frontier alternatives, kept with their verdicts for later evidence: Herders by region: the Eurasian steppe, Arabia and the Sahara, East Africa's and the Sahel's cattle herders, the high plateaus of Tibet and the Andes (universality), Herders by animal: cattle, camels, horses, sheep and goats, reindeer, yaks and llamas (necessity, independence, universality), Transhumant against fully nomadic herders (necessity, independence).","data":{"schema":"meaning-model-carve/v1","part":"synthesis","cutId":"carve.concept.humanity.means.habitat.mobile.herders","conceptId":"concept.humanity.means.habitat.mobile.herders","form":"processes","cutRecorded":false,"parts":[],"process":"h.habitat.mobile.herders"}}

{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"Range in Northern America is kept whole, as a kind of Range in the Americas: No carve pays now. The Arctic split passes the tests, but outside the Arctic the range has been full since about 10,000 BCE, so a part would sit flat for twelve thousand years, and the Arctic's two steps (Paleo-Inuit from about 2500 BCE, Thule from about 1250) already show in the whole. Reopen if range is redefined to count how intensively land is used, or if dated site series for the Arctic and the Great Basin are entered. (passed: The Arctic and the land south of it)

