{"schema":"meaning-model-understanding-note/v1","kind":"decision","text":"Hunger is kept whole, as a kind of Causes of death: No carve pays now. Famine against chronic hunger is the natural split, but most deaths in both are certified as infections, and no series separates them before the twentieth century, so the chronic part would be the whole's level relabelled. The regional split would show Asia's famines giving way to Africa's, but it needs regional famine tolls the model has only as Event notes. Reopen when famine tolls by region and decade are entered (Ó Gráda's and Devereux's lists), or if the causes of death are carved so that hunger as an underlying cause can be counted beside infection.

How the parts make the whole work: Kept whole. The famine spikes are already dated values of the whole, each with its Event (the El Niño famines, the Great Leap famine, Ethiopia's famines). The chronic level is the slow fall beneath them. A split would rest on the attribution of deaths between hunger and infection, which the sources do not make before the twentieth century (EvidenceUnderdetermination#999b).

